\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 ANTIHUNTER DIGI NODE\
\fs28 TIER 2 \'96 COMPLETE PARTS KIT
\f0\b0\fs22 \cf1 \
\
Every part needed to build a finished node, as it comes from the supplier. Nothing is soldered and nothing is flashed.\
\
\
\f1\b IN THE BOX
\f0\b0 \
\
Bare 82 mm PCB, all modules and headers, 8 GB microSD\
Printed enclosure, TPU seals, all M3 hardware and standoffs\
SMA antennas, U.FL pigtails and bulkheads, passive ceramic GPS antenna\
Fan, thermal switch, power switch, UPS charger board, JST terminals and cables\
\
You supply: two 18650 cells, soldering tools.\
\
\
\f1\b BUILD IT
\f0\b0 \
\
1. Work through the assembly manual end to end. It has photographed steps for the soldering, the connectors, the enclosure, the SD card and the power wiring:\
\
\f1\b github.com/lukeswitz/AntiHunter \'96 hw folder, Antihunter-DIGINODE-AssemblyManual.pdf
\f0\b0 \
\
2. Two modules need a header modification first, covered on page 6 of that manual: the RTC ships with female headers, and some tamper sensors ship with inverted 90 degree headers.\
\
3. Fit the SD card before you close the case. The slot is not reachable once the PCB is mounted.\
\
\
\f1\b FLASH IT
\f0\b0 \
\
4. Flash the Heltec V3.2 or T114 with the latest stable Meshtastic from flasher.meshtastic.org, then set the serial module: Enabled, mode TEXTMSG, baud 115200, pins 19 RX / 20 TX on Heltec V3 or 10 RX / 9 TX on T114. Without this the node and the radio cannot talk.\
\
5. Flash AntiHunter on the ESP32 over USB. Web flasher: lukeswitz.github.io/AntiHunter. Pick Full for the web UI, or Headless for quiet field ops.\
\
6. Set the LoRa region, change the Bluetooth pairing pin, and make your own encrypted channel primary with the public default off.\
\
7. Full firmware: join the \f1\b Antihunter\f0\b0  WiFi AP, password \f1\b antihunt3r123\f0\b0 , open http://192.168.4.1 and change those credentials first.\
\
\
\f1\b POWER
\f0\b0 \
\
Regulated 5 V only, from USB or the UPS board. Never wire cells or an unregulated supply to the PCB. A 2 A fast-blow fuse in the battery line is recommended and is not supplied. One USB cable at a time: the ESP32 and the radio share the power rails.\
\
\
\f1\b THE FULL GUIDE
\f0\b0 \
\
Unboxing to deployment, antennas, all the detectors, the vibration sensor, mesh commands and Command Center:\
\
\f1\b github.com/lukeswitz/AntiHunter/blob/main/docs/AntiHunter-Operators-Guide.pdf
\f0\b0 \
\
Firmware, docs, issues: github.com/lukeswitz/AntiHunter\
